From ba5cac0ed4ab6fdc7467ce256801a3bafa761ef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sl91994 <112153975+sl91994@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 19:14:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix panic in the Modular RLE fast path when LZ77 is disabled
 (#912)

`Histograms::is_rle()` asks whether every LZ77 copy has distance 1 by inspecting
the histogram of the LZ77 distance cluster, but never checked whether LZ77 is
enabled. With LZ77 disabled there is no distance cluster and `lz_dist_cluster`
stays 0, so `is_rle()` inspected cluster 0 instead -- a real pixel-data
histogram. Any stream whose cluster 0 codes the constant symbol 1 with a
split-exponent-zero uint config was therefore reported as RLE.

Together with a single Gradient leaf and prefix codes -- the rest of what
`can_decode_fast_lossless()` requires, and an entirely ordinary minimal Modular
stream -- this made `decode_modular_subbitstream()` take the RLE fast path,
where `decode_fast_lossless()` unwraps `min_symbol`, `min_length` and
`lz77_length_uint`. All three are `None` without LZ77, so decoding such a file
panicked. The very same stream decodes without any error on the normal path, so
this is a valid input that only the fast path mishandles.

Check `lz77_params.enabled` in `is_rle()` and report such histograms as not RLE.
This matches the other fast paths in the crate -- `can_use_config_420_fast_path()`
and `run_on_specialized_tree()` already gate on the same flag -- and leaves
streams that legitimately use the RLE fast path, which have LZ77 enabled,
unaffected.

Add two test files. Both are complete codestreams for the same 8x8 image, a
single Modular frame whose three colour channels are coded in the LfGlobal
section with one Gradient leaf and a constant residual, and they differ only in
whether LZ77 is enabled in the pixel histograms.
`modular_rle_fast_path_without_lz77.jxl` is the stream described above: it used
to panic, and must now decode on the normal path.
`modular_rle_fast_path.jxl` codes the same image as a genuine RLE stream, so it
still takes the fast path and must decode to the very same pixels.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Co-authored-by: Luca Versari <veluca93@gmail.com>

Local backport scope: production changes only. Upstream regression tests,
fixtures, and test-only harness changes are intentionally omitted. The
original commit message above describes the full upstream change.

diff --git a/jxl/src/entropy_coding/decode.rs b/jxl/src/entropy_coding/decode.rs
index eb2b68f0f..cd2819448 100644
--- a/jxl/src/entropy_coding/decode.rs
+++ b/jxl/src/entropy_coding/decode.rs
@@ -569,7 +569,14 @@ impl Histograms {
         &self.codes
     }
 
+    /// Whether every LZ77 copy has distance 1, i.e. the stream is a plain run-length
+    /// encoding. False without LZ77: there is no distance cluster then (`lz_dist_cluster`
+    /// falls back to cluster 0, which holds real data), and the parameters an RLE decoder
+    /// needs (`min_symbol`, `min_length`, `lz77_length_uint`) are `None`.
     pub fn is_rle(&self) -> bool {
+        if !self.lz77_params.enabled {
+            return false;
+        }
         let lz_dist_cluster = self.lz_dist_cluster as usize;
         let lz_conf = &self.uint_configs[lz_dist_cluster];
         self.codes.single_symbol(lz_dist_cluster) == Some(1) && lz_conf.is_split_exponent_zero()
